  (function () {
    var el = document.getElementById("dm-dateline");
    if (!el) return;
    var d = new Date(),
      p = function (n) {
        return String(n).padStart(2, "0");
      };
    el.textContent =
      d.getUTCFullYear() +
      "-" +
      p(d.getUTCMonth() + 1) +
      "-" +
      p(d.getUTCDate()) +
      " " +
      p(d.getUTCHours()) +
      ":" +
      p(d.getUTCMinutes()) +
      " UTC";
  })();
</script><script>
  (function () {
    var toggle = document.getElementById("dm-mobile-toggle");
    var menu = document.getElementById("dm-mobile-menu");
    if (!toggle || !menu) return;
    var menuIcon = toggle.querySelector('[data-icon="menu"]');
    var closeIcon = toggle.querySelector('[data-icon="close"]');
    toggle.addEventListener("click", function () {
      var open = menu.classList.toggle("hidden") === false;
      toggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", open ? "true" : "false");
      if (menuIcon) menuIcon.classList.toggle("hidden", open);
      if (closeIcon) closeIcon.classList.toggle("hidden", !open);
    });
    menu.querySelectorAll("a").forEach(function (link) {
      link.addEventListener("click", function () {
        menu.classList.add("hidden");
        toggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
        if (menuIcon) menuIcon.classList.remove("hidden");
        if (closeIcon) closeIcon.classList.add("hidden");
      });
    });
  })();
</script><main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6"><div><section class="border-b border-border pb-10"><div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_380px]"><a href="/blog/meta-muse-apple-watch-wear-os-what-you-get" class="group block"><div class="mb-4 aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden bg-muted"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/5a045ad5-055c-47d0-81e6-dcf77e739e5a.webp" alt="Meta Muse Lands on Apple Watch and Wear OS: What You Get" width="960" height="540" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="sync" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.03]"></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Agents</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 10, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h2 class="mt-2 text-balance font-serif text-3xl font-bold leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent sm:text-4xl">Meta Muse Lands on Apple Watch and Wear OS: What You Get</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Meta brought its Muse AI agent to Apple Watch and Wear OS with voice, text and dictation. What the wrist app does, what the plans cost, and where it works.</p></a><div class="flex flex-col gap-6 border-t border-border pt-6 lg:border-t-0 lg:pt-0"><a href="/blog/gemini-4-carbon-pricing-vs-claude-fable-5-2-real-math" class="group flex gap-4"><div class="h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/307433bd-db9b-48f2-b901-e2ebfb425bca.webp" alt="Gemini 4 Carbon Pricing vs Claude Fable 5.2: The Real Math" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">AI Models</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 10, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>5 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1 line-clamp-3 font-serif text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Gemini 4 Carbon Pricing vs Claude Fable 5.2: The Real Math</h3></div></a><a href="/blog/apple-charges-49-99-for-extra-apple-intelligence-in-logic-pro" class="group flex gap-4"><div class="h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/21ac06b0-ccfa-4ea0-b9a3-ed53101900b2.webp" alt="Apple Charges $49.99 for Extra Apple Intelligence in Logic Pro" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Industry</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 10, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1 line-clamp-3 font-serif text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Apple Charges $49.99 for Extra Apple Intelligence in Logic Pro</h3></div></a></div></div></section><div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_280px]"><section><p class="dm-overline">Latest</p><div class="mt-2"><a href="/blog/prompt-ensembles-only-beat-self-consistency-when-errors-differ" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">AI Models</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 09, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Prompt Ensembles Only Beat Self-Consistency When Errors Differ</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">A simulation puts five varied prompts at 21/24 and five samples of one prompt at 15/24 on the same budget. The gain vanishes when errors correlate.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/469a18cb-3a3f-48dd-becc-a39e41c21508.webp" alt="Prompt Ensembles Only Beat Self-Consistency When Errors Differ" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/anthropic-buys-3-4b-of-gas-turbines-for-1-7gw-of-power" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Infrastructure</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 09, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>5 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Anthropic Buys $3.4B of Gas Turbines for 1.7GW of Power</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Anthropic is buying Caterpillar generators rated up to 1.7GW, breaking from its rent-don&#39;t-own pattern as turbine backlogs stretch into the 2030s.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/1d71f732-b310-4052-a6b3-a4b69486f852.webp" alt="Anthropic Buys $3.4B of Gas Turbines for 1.7GW of Power" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/claude-md-edits-break-prompt-caching-a-10x-worked-example" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Dev Tools</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 09, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">CLAUDE.md Edits Break Prompt Caching: A 10x Worked Example</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">A new guide puts CLAUDE.md at the front of the cache prefix: edit it mid-session and the same 4,000 tokens cost about 10x more across 40 turns.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/20203ebb-78bd-4c1d-8182-1a0944893fc3.webp" alt="CLAUDE.md Edits Break Prompt Caching: A 10x Worked Example" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/apples-agentic-siri-what-gurman-says-lands-in-ios-27-3" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Agents</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 09, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Apple&#39;s Agentic Siri: What Gurman Says Lands in iOS 27.3</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Gurman reports Siri gets fine-grained control of Apple&#39;s own apps in iOS 27.3, third-party apps in spring. What&#39;s checkable and what Apple hasn&#39;t confirmed.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/9dbf7dad-3e72-4cc1-8891-e4566079aaeb.webp" alt="Apple's Agentic Siri: What Gurman Says Lands in iOS 27.3" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/cursor-voice-chat-for-agents-what-it-does-where-it-stops" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Dev Tools</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 08, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Cursor Voice Chat for Agents: What It Does, Where It Stops</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Cursor shipped two-way voice chat with coding agents on 6 November. It runs on Grok Voice, is blocked for API-key sessions, and the daily limit is unpublished.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/8a997d41-f9f1-4354-b544-382aa9038b2f.webp" alt="Cursor Voice Chat for Agents: What It Does, Where It Stops" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/ante-vs-claude-code-is-a-15mb-offline-agent-enough" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Dev Tools</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 07, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Ante vs Claude Code: Is a 15MB Offline Agent Enough?</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">A week-long comparison puts Ante&#39;s single Rust binary against Claude Code: far smaller footprint and offline models, but beta bugs and no Windows.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/47097bc4-78c1-4880-ab65-a1b6e7dacb34.webp" alt="Ante vs Claude Code: Is a 15MB Offline Agent Enough?" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/two-reports-show-ai-outrunning-the-humans-who-check-it" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Industry</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 07, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>6 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Two Reports Show AI Outrunning the Humans Who Check It</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">METR says Anthropic&#39;s models improve twice as fast as a year ago, mostly because of AI. Days later: 948 Linux exploits in 30 hours for $1.2M.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/30ea5dcf-73ea-4c3b-99e2-3395cb44dcd0.webp" alt="Two Reports Show AI Outrunning the Humans Who Check It" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/one-rule-tactics-i-shipped-a-tactics-puzzle-where-every-enemy-follows-one-rule" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Dev Tools</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 07, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>2 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">One-Rule Tactics: I shipped a tactics puzzle where every enemy follows one rule</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">My first Android game is live on Google Play: a free, offline 5×5 tactics puzzle where enemies always step toward you, so you win by luring them into rocks, pits and each other.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/37b08c89-7c3f-4d04-b3cb-839e6225ea06.webp" alt="One-Rule Tactics: I shipped a tactics puzzle where every enemy follows one rule" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/gemini-omni-1-2-flash-is-ga-a-15-second-clip-costs-1-04" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">AI Models</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 07, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash Is GA: A 15-Second Clip Costs $1.04</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Google&#39;s video model went GA on November 5 with a 30 percent price cut. What a 15-second clip really costs, and how it compares to Veo 3.1 and Runway.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/d14819ec-5769-45ae-86e7-95d7b18c5322.webp" alt="Gemini Omni 1.2 Flash Is GA: A 15-Second Clip Costs $1.04" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/vercel-tracing-is-ga-on-by-default-for-nextjs-16-5" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Infrastructure</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 06, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>3 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Vercel Tracing Is GA, On by Default for Next.js 16.5</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Vercel Tracing hit GA on all plans. New Next.js 16.5 projects trace 100% of requests by default, and Pro retention jumped from 1 day to 14 days.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/b6cd9759-92af-470c-b720-a580ef117880.webp" alt="Vercel Tracing Is GA, On by Default for Next.js 16.5" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/ai-code-passes-tests-but-only-18-4-percent-secure" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Agents</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 06, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>6 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">AI Code Passes Tests but Only 18.4% of It Is Secure</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">A 145-CVE benchmark found Claude Code passed 74.0% of functional tests but wrote secure code on just 18.4%. Naming the safeguard moved the number.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/003f5ae9-d8d2-44cc-9984-c9de10444e2c.webp" alt="AI Code Passes Tests but Only 18.4% of It Is Secure" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/parallax-beta-8-shows-a-real-iphone-agents-cant-tap-it" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">Dev Tools</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 06, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Parallax beta.8 Shows a Real iPhone — Agents Can&#39;t Tap It</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Parallax now streams a plugged-in iPhone beside a Galaxy S24, and beta.7 cut agent taps from 14s to under a second on Android hardware. Here is the catch.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/e80640aa-cc46-45f9-8877-67b723e2f3f4.webp" alt="Parallax beta.8 Shows a Real iPhone — Agents Can't Tap It" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a><a href="/blog/kimi-k3-1-pro-weights-are-open-can-you-actually-run-it" class="group flex items-start justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border py-5 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground"><span class="text-accent">AI Models</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Nov 05, 2026</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>4 min read</span></div><h3 class="mt-1.5 font-serif text-xl font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors group-hover:text-accent">Kimi K3.1 Pro Weights Are Open. Can You Actually Run It?</h3><p class="mt-1.5 line-clamp-2 max-w-2xl text-sm text-muted-foreground">Moonshot opened Kimi K3.1 Pro&#39;s weights: 2.8T parameters, a 1.56 TB download, and 8+ B300-class GPUs to self-host. The hosted API is still the real route.</p></div><div class="hidden h-20 w-28 shrink-0 overflow-hidden bg-muted sm:block"><img src="https://img.nextfuture.io.vn/nextfuture/2026/11/874e8bdd-9dc9-46cf-9ecd-e9242f4eb76c.webp" alt="Kimi K3.1 Pro Weights Are Open. Can You Actually Run It?" width="224" height="160" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 ease-out group-hover:scale-[1.05]"></div></a></div></section><aside aria-labelledby="trending-heading"><p class="dm-overline" id="trending-heading">Trending this week</p><ol class="mt-4"><li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-border py-4 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><span class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-border">01</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Dev Tools</div><a href="/blog/one-rule-tactics-i-shipped-a-tactics-puzzle-where-every-enemy-follows-one-rule" class="mt-1 block font-serif text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent">One-Rule Tactics: I shipped a tactics puzzle where every enemy follows one rule</a></div></li><li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-border py-4 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><span class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-border">02</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">AI Models</div><a href="/blog/kimi-k3-1-pro-weights-are-open-can-you-actually-run-it" class="mt-1 block font-serif text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent">Kimi K3.1 Pro Weights Are Open. Can You Actually Run It?</a></div></li><li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-border py-4 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><span class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-border">03</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">AI Models</div><a href="/blog/gpt-6-cyber-hits-critical-as-agent-shell-gates-still-leak" class="mt-1 block font-serif text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent">GPT-6 Cyber Hits Critical as Agent Shell Gates Still Leak</a></div></li><li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-border py-4 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><span class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-border">04</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">Industry</div><a href="/blog/gemini-for-home-lands-in-at-t-s-30-a-month-security-plan" class="mt-1 block font-serif text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent">Gemini for Home Lands in AT&amp;T&#39;s $30-a-Month Security Plan</a></div></li><li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-border py-4 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><span class="font-mono text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums text-border">05</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="font-mono text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">AI Models</div><a href="/blog/anthropic-flashprove-aims-to-prove-which-model-answered" class="mt-1 block font-serif text-sm font-semibold leading-snug text-foreground transition-colors hover:text-accent">Anthropic&#39;s FlashProve Aims to Prove Which Model Answered</a></div></li></ol></aside></div></div></main><footer class="border-t border-border bg-background"><div class="mx-au